Date: Tue, 19 Jan 93 11:21:09 CST
From: eder@hsvaic.boeing.com (Dani Eder)
Subject: Re:  PPL: Why Not Let Convicts Run the Police?

There are already private databases that can serve to ostracise
a person based on his/her past actions.  One to which I used
to belong was a tenant database.  If one of my tenants didn't
pay rent on time or trashed the place, I was supposed to report
this to the agency.  In return I could find out about the rental
history of prospective new tenants.  The value of this service to
landlords is obvious.  Another such system is used by some doctors
to track patients who have sued a previous doctor.  With
malpractice insurance so expensive, avoiding future suits is of
great value.  Of course, most of us are familiar with the State-run
systems that track driving incidents like traffic tickets.  The
state is willing to take back your driving license and auto insurance
companies are willing to deny you insurance based on your driving
history, i.e. your 'driving reputation'.

Dani Eder

